   "instructions": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><p>This is a real FPTU <b>SU26 · FE · RE</b> paper for <b>CSD201</b>, shown as the original page images (one page per question).</p><ul><li>Multiple-choice page: write the letter(s) you choose and one line of reasoning.</li><li>Practical / essay page: write your answer or solution; you may attach a photo of your work.</li><li>AI grading compares your answer with the page image; treat the score as practice feedback, not an official mark.</li></ul><p><b>Notes on the paper / Ghi chú kèm đề:</b></p><pre>CSD201 SU26 FE RE\n\nCSD201 SU26 FE RE Questions​\nThis document contains a set of multiple-choice questions from a CSD201 exam. The questions cover fundamental data structures such as singly and doubly linked lists, time complexities of node insertion, operations on linked lists, and the applicability of binary search algorithms.\n\nCSD201 SU26 FE RE Questions​\n\nCâu 1\nSelect the statement that is most correct.\nBasically, the complexity of inserting new element before a given node in the middle of a singly linked lists is\nA. O(n^2)\nB. O(1)\nC. O(log n)\nD. O\n\nCâu 2\nSelect the statement that is most correct.\nSuppose we are considering a doubly linked list which has at least 2 nodes. What does the java code snippet below do?\nNode f = tail.prev; // prev is a link to predecessor node\nNode q = new Node(x);\nq.prev = f; q.next = tail;\nf.next = q; tail.prev = q;\nA. It creates new node with value x at the middle of the list.\nB. It inserts new node with value x after the last node.\nC. It replaces the last node with new node with value x.\nD. It inserts new node with value x before the last node.\n\nCâu 3\nSelect the statement that is most correct.\nBasically, the complexity of inserting a node after a given node in a singly linked lists is\nA. O\nB. O(1)\nC. O(log n)\nD. O(n^2)\n\nCâu 4\nConsider the fun() method in a singly linked list below:\nvoid fun()\n{ if (isEmpty()) return;\nif (head == tail)\nhead = tail = null;\nelse head = head.next;\n}\nSpecify the correct statement about the fun() method in the code above (choose the most suitable one).\nA. It removes the last element of the list\nB. It removes the first element of the list\nC. It removes the second element of the list\nD. It returns the first element of the list\n\nCâu 5\nBinary search algorithm cannot be applied to\nA. sorted linear array\nB. sorted singly linked list\nC. Binary search tree\nNhấn để mở rộng...</pre></div><div class=\"ml-vi\"><p>Đây là đề <b>SU26 · FE · Thi lại</b> thật của FPTU môn <b>CSD201</b>, hiển thị nguyên ảnh trang đề gốc (mỗi trang là một câu).</p><ul><li>Trang trắc nghiệm: ghi chữ cái đáp án bạn chọn và một dòng lý do.</li><li>Trang thực hành / tự luận: viết bài làm hoặc lời giải; có thể đính kèm ảnh bài làm.</li><li>AI chấm bằng cách so bài làm với ảnh đề — điểm chỉ để luyện tập, không phải điểm chính thức.</li></ul><p><b>Notes on the paper / Ghi chú kèm đề:</b></p><pre>CSD201 SU26 FE RE\n\nCSD201 SU26 FE RE Questions​\nThis document contains a set of multiple-choice questions from a CSD201 exam. The questions cover fundamental data structures such as singly and doubly linked lists, time complexities of node insertion, operations on linked lists, and the applicability of binary search algorithms.\n\nCSD201 SU26 FE RE Questions​\n\nCâu 1\nSelect the statement that is most correct.\nBasically, the complexity of inserting new element before a given node in the middle of a singly linked lists is\nA. O(n^2)\nB. O(1)\nC. O(log n)\nD. O\n\nCâu 2\nSelect the statement that is most correct.\nSuppose we are considering a doubly linked list which has at least 2 nodes. What does the java code snippet below do?\nNode f = tail.prev; // prev is a link to predecessor node\nNode q = new Node(x);\nq.prev = f; q.next = tail;\nf.next = q; tail.prev = q;\nA. It creates new node with value x at the middle of the list.\nB. It inserts new node with value x after the last node.\nC. It replaces the last node with new node with value x.\nD. It inserts new node with value x before the last node.\n\nCâu 3\nSelect the statement that is most correct.\nBasically, the complexity of inserting a node after a given node in a singly linked lists is\nA. O\nB. O(1)\nC. O(log n)\nD. O(n^2)\n\nCâu 4\nConsider the fun() method in a singly linked list below:\nvoid fun()\n{ if (isEmpty()) return;\nif (head == tail)\nhead = tail = null;\nelse head = head.next;\n}\nSpecify the correct statement about the fun() method in the code above (choose the most suitable one).\nA. It removes the last element of the list\nB. It removes the first element of the list\nC. It removes the second element of the list\nD. It returns the first element of the list\n\nCâu 5\nBinary search algorithm cannot be applied to\nA. sorted linear array\nB. sorted singly linked list\nC. Binary search tree\nNhấn để mở rộng...</pre></div>",
